A command-line interface for searching Mozilla codebases using searchfox.org.

Examples:
  searchfox-cli -q AudioStream
  searchfox-cli -q AudioStream -C -l 10
  searchfox-cli -q '^Audio.*' -r
  searchfox-cli -q AudioStream -p ^dom/media
  searchfox-cli -p PContent.ipdl  # Search for files by path only
  searchfox-cli --get-file dom/media/AudioStream.h
  searchfox-cli --symbol AudioContext
  searchfox-cli --symbol 'AudioContext::CreateGain'
  searchfox-cli --id main
  searchfox-cli -q 'path:dom/media AudioStream'
  searchfox-cli -q 'symbol:AudioContext' --context 3
  searchfox-cli --define 'AudioContext::CreateGain'
  searchfox-cli --calls-from 'mozilla::dom::AudioContext::CreateGain' --depth 2
  searchfox-cli --calls-to 'mozilla::dom::AudioContext::CreateGain' --depth 3
  searchfox-cli --calls-between 'AudioContext,AudioNode' --depth 2

Usage: searchfox-cli [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -q, --query <QUERY>
          Search query string

  -R, --repo <REPO>
          Repository to search in. Available repositories:
            mozilla-central (default) - Main Firefox development
            autoland - Integration repository
            mozilla-beta - Beta release branch
            mozilla-release - Release branch
            mozilla-esr115 - ESR 115 branch
            mozilla-esr128 - ESR 128 branch
            mozilla-esr140 - ESR 140 branch
            comm-central - Thunderbird development
          
          [default: mozilla-central]

  -p, --path <PATH>
          Filter search results by file path prefix or search for files by path pattern.
          Use regex patterns to match specific directories or files.
          Can be used alone to search for files without a query.
          Examples:
            -p ^dom/media (with query) - filters results to files starting with dom/media/
            -p PContent.ipdl (alone) - finds all files matching PContent.ipdl

  -C, --case
          Enable case-sensitive search

  -r, --regexp
          Enable regular expression search mode.
          Allows using regex patterns in the query string.
          Example: '^Audio.*' matches identifiers starting with 'Audio'

  -l, --limit <LIMIT>
          Maximum number of results to display
          
          [default: 50]

      --get-file <GET_FILE>
          Fetch and display the contents of a specific file from the repository.
          Provide the file path relative to the repository root.
          Example: --get-file dom/media/AudioStream.h

      --context <CONTEXT>
          Show N lines of context above and below each match.
          Only works with text: or re: queries.
          Example: --context 3

      --symbol <SYMBOL>
          Search for symbol definitions using searchfox's symbol indexing.
          Uses symbol: query syntax internally.
          Example: --symbol AudioContext

      --id <ID>
          Search for exact identifier matches (not prefix-based).
          Uses id: query syntax internally.
          Example: --id main

      --define <DEFINE>
          Find the definition of a symbol using searchfox's structured data.
          Searches for symbol definitions and class/struct declarations.
          Displays the complete method/function body or class declaration.
          Example: --define 'AudioContext::CreateGain' or --define 'AudioContext'

      --log-requests
          Log all HTTP requests made to searchfox with detailed timing information:
          - Request start/end timestamps
          - Response size and duration
          - Network latency measurement via ping
          Useful for performance analysis and infrastructure planning

      --cpp
          Filter results to C++ files only (.cc, .cpp, .h, .hh, .hpp)

      --c
          Filter results to C files only (.c, .h)

      --webidl
          Filter results to WebIDL files only (.webidl)

      --js
          Filter results to JavaScript files only (.js, .mjs, .ts, .cjs, .jsx, .tsx)

      --calls-from <CALLS_FROM>
          Search for functions called by the specified symbol using call graph analysis.
          Example: --calls-from 'mozilla::dom::AudioContext::CreateGain'

      --calls-to <CALLS_TO>
          Search for functions that call the specified symbol using call graph analysis.
          Example: --calls-to 'mozilla::dom::AudioContext::CreateGain'

      --calls-between <CALLS_BETWEEN>
          Find function calls between two symbols or classes.
          Example: --calls-between 'AudioContext,AudioNode'

      --depth <DEPTH>
          Set the depth of traversal for call graph searches. Higher values show more indirect calls.
          Example: --depth 3
          
          [default: 2]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
